osku@mpoli.fi (Osku Salerma) writes:

>What ways are there to change the status of the item, I.e from normal to
>blessed and so on. I only know about dipping in holy water, but that
>doesn't work with scrolls and spellbooks, and anyway, I never know what
>water I have, so I wouldn't even know what it would do. It's so
>difficult to try to keep your pet with you, that I never bother to do
>it. And altars arent that common, so I have no means to determine the
>status of anything..

No, dipping in (un)holy water will work for scrolls and books as well
as for other items. If you dip a scroll in

holy water:	it will get blessed,
unholy water:	it will get cursed,
uncursed water:	it will become a blank scroll.

By the way, I don't think it's difficult to keep your pet with you at
all. You only have to wait at the stairs once in a while. This is fixed
as soon as you get hold of a magic whistle, which aren't all that
uncommon.

As for altars, that's another thing. You can be sure there is one in
the Mine Town, but I have had games in which I had only one other one
in the entire dungeon. For me, this is the most important reason to
keep my pet (even more important than robbing stores).

As for thederminig the holy/unholy/uncursed state of water, when you
start seeing more than two of the same in one slot in your inventory
(clear potions, that is), you can be pretty sure it's uncursed water.
If you have: a) 5 clear potions b) 1 clear potion c) 1 clear potion,
then (a) is uncursed, with a certainness of some 90%.

